From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: apply a changed default home screen on an upgrade

0010 named what belongs on the home screen, and the first installation over an
existing data image showed none of it: the first cell still held the browser
and nothing else ("首屏幕第一格是浏览器，其他应用都没有", user, 2026-10-20).
The layout is read by loadDefaultFavoritesIfNecessary(), which fills a database
that was just created; a database that already exists is never seeded again, so
a release that changes the layout changes nothing for anyone who already has
the system.

The database version is what this file uses to decide that question, and
falling out of the switch in onUpgrade is how it already starts over when a
database cannot be carried forward. 27 now does that instead of returning, and
28 is the version a carried-forward database ends at.

This discards a home screen somebody arranged by hand, which is why the version
moves only in a release that changes the default layout -- and why it moves now:
the arrangement a reader could have made on 0010's layout is the one this
release is fixing. Every database this project has written is at 27, so every
device re-seeds once, here.

diff --git a/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json b/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
index 3c1b64f..988978c 100644
--- a/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
+++ b/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
@@ -2,7 +2,11 @@
   // Note: Comments are not supported in JSON schema, but android parser is lenient.
 
   // Maximum DB version supported by this schema
-  "version" : 27,
+  "version" : 28,
+
+  // PW3: 28 only re-seeds the workspace, it does not change the tables, so a
+  // database written by it is read by 27 as it stands.
+  "downgrade_to_27" : [],
 
   // Downgrade from 27 to 26. Empty array indicates, the DB is compatible
   "downgrade_to_26" : [],
diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
index b31df98..0e387c4 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
@@ -85,7 +85,10 @@ public class LauncherProvider extends ContentProvider {
     /**
      * Represents the schema of the database. Changes in scheme need not be backwards compatible.
      */
-    public static final int SCHEMA_VERSION = 27;
+    /* PW3: 28 because the default home screen changed. The version is what
+     * decides whether a workspace seeded by an older release is carried
+     * forward or seeded again (onUpgrade below). */
+    public static final int SCHEMA_VERSION = 28;
 
     public static final String AUTHORITY = (BuildConfig.APPLICATION_ID + ".settings").intern();
 
@@ -826,6 +829,21 @@ public class LauncherProvider extends ContentProvider {
                         break;
                     }
                 case 27:
+                    // PW3: the default home screen changed. A workspace that
+                    // was seeded before it keeps what it was seeded with --
+                    // loadDefaultFavoritesIfNecessary() fills a database that
+                    // was just created, and nothing re-reads the layout
+                    // afterwards -- so installing a release over an existing
+                    // data image came up with the previous home screen
+                    // ("首屏幕第一格是浏览器，其他应用都没有", user,
+                    // 2026-10-20). Leaving the switch here is this file's own
+                    // way of starting over when a database cannot be carried
+                    // forward: the next load seeds it from
+                    // default_workspace_5x6.xml again. It discards an
+                    // arrangement made by hand, so SCHEMA_VERSION moves only
+                    // in a release that changes the default layout.
+                    break;
+                case 28:
                     // DB Upgraded successfully
                     return;
             }
